# Requests for VS Code "REST Client" or JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Run them top to bottom; the login response token has to be copied into @token.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:5000
@token = paste-access-token-here

### 0. Health (public)
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Register a user
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "Bob-Str0ng-Pass!"
}

### 2. Login - returns the JWT
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Alice-Str0ng-Pass!"
}

### 3. Protected endpoint WITHOUT a token -> 401
GET {{base}}/api/data

### 4. Protected endpoint WITH the token -> 200
GET {{base}}/api/data?limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Search (parameterised LIKE) -> 200
GET {{base}}/api/data?q=secure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Create a post (authenticated write)
POST {{base}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My first post",
  "body": "Written over a JWT-protected endpoint."
}

### 7. XSS payload gets escaped on the way out
POST {{base}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "<script>alert('xss')</script>",
  "body": "<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>"
}

### 8. Who am I + verified token claims
GET {{base}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. SQL injection attempt in the login body -> 401
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice' OR '1'='1",
  "password": "x"
}

### 10. SQL injection attempt in the search parameter -> 200, zero rows
GET {{base}}/api/data?q=%27%20OR%201%3D1%20--
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
